Z||000002||theogre||02-22-2001||08:26 PM||||I had trouble getting some pages pushed to the server. Some pages were unreachable for several hours. I just tested it and it worked ok for me now.<P>The first page looks the same but is not. That page has had internal changes mainly to block the spam bots.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> The java animated dots next to the links on the main page have been fixed and tweeked a bit. (Depending on just when you looked they weren't loading for awhile. The Java applet and server are crabby about how the file is named case wise.)<P>The rest of the main cave, other than the tech centre has been updated to use the new style sheet. The main cave and Fiero cave now look similar. The main cave will change some when I find a new background I like. For the time being the sandy looking one fits in with the rest ok.<P>I haven't decided what I'm going to do with the tech area. I may remove it or just the stuff that's win95 centric. There are allot of people still using win95 so I haven't decided. It will probably stay untill I need the space.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||02-23-2001||07:57 PM||||I fixed a few more things late last night.... the favorites icon used by IE 5 and later works for both the main cave and the fiero cave. (diferant icons for each.) It even works thru Proxy servers.<P>Is anyone using the IE "channel" for off line reading? If people are actually interested in that I'll keep it. Other wise I'm not going to update it anymore and I may dump it. The site cannot be used offline without the channel. (No, The built in offline viewing in IE 5.x won't work right...)<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 02-23-2001).]||||reg||1
